    {
        "content": "<p>(Coming from <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Transparency.20problem.20with.20quaternions/near/620090442\">#mathlib4 &gt; Transparency problem with quaternions @ 💬</a>)</p>",
        "id": 620124161,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788105367
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The uninformative error is apparently due to using the notation/macro <code>tsze</code> in the file instead of writing out <code>TrivSqZeroExt</code> in full.<br>\nRemoving the local notation, the error line 914 is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthesize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">LinearMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CompatibleSMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TrivSqZeroExt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 620125491,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1788106193
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(Dropping the <code>local</code> from the <code>local notation</code> defining <code>tsze</code> also changes the error message to a reasonable one. I don’t really get why, but it looks like the pretty-printer is not happy with using a private notation in the error message?)</p>",
        "id": 620126107,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1788106646
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yes this is a problem that has been happening</p>",
