    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/TrivSqZeroExt.20as.20a.202-field.20structure/near/620175296\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>you can use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Homeomorph.t2Space#doc\">docs#Homeomorph.t2Space</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>But then I have absolutely no idea how to show that the <code>equivProd</code> I defined in the PR is a homeomorphism. There are absolutely no lemmas allowing me to show that custom structure fields are continuous.</p>\n<p>Although the following instance <em>does</em> work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instTopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tsze</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induced</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‹_›</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induced</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‹_›</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 620180318,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788141238
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- The canonical homeomorphism between `TrivSqZeroExt R M` and `R × M`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">homeomorphProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tsze</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">__</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">equivProd</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">equivProd</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_prodMk</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- how???</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">continuous_invFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">equivProd</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 620180523,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788141342
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You should add the lemmas <code>continuous_fst</code> and <code>continuous_snd</code> first</p>",
        "id": 620180556,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788141358
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you can probably just copy what is done for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=continuous_fst#doc\">docs#continuous_fst</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=continuous_snd#doc\">docs#continuous_snd</a></p>",
        "id": 620180598,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788141377
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I found that adding <code>public import Mathlib.Topology.Homeomorph.TransferInstance</code> and using the following works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tsze</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">equivProd</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">topologicalSpace</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- The canonical homeomorphism between `TrivSqZeroExt R M` and `R × M`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">homeomorphProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tsze</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">equivProd</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">homeomorph</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But is transferring the instances this way a good idea?</p>",
        "id": 620182440,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788141977
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(This has been pushed to the PR)</p>",
        "id": 620183072,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Tan",
        "timestamp": 1788142319
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it doesn't seem like a bad idea</p>",
